{"id": "450bdd1a-db25-4d38-83e6-18b03806490d", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T23:18:18.532346", "source": "user", "parent_id": "57f9dca9-7a6b-4659-af14-f9b851ea557d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task: the deliverable is a final experiment design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility) for identifying rare patterns in a tabular dataset using Docta. No experimental execution is required and repositories/compute are not strictly needed, but a grounded design is. For this first step, please inspect the /workspace repository only and report back: (1) what Docta is in this repo — its API, documented capabilities, and any modules or documentation related to detecting rare/long-tail/hard-sample patterns (e.g., README, examples, config files, entry points); (2) how tabular data is supported, if at all (dataset loaders, input formats, preprocessing); (3) any examples or tests showing Docta's typical input/output and workflow; (4) any dependencies or environment assumptions. Then propose a tentative experiment-design approach: what the experiment would aim to demonstrate about rare-pattern identification, what dataset/architecture of the design you'd use, what controls and metrics you'd include, and clearly list the consequential assumptions and uncertainties (e.g., assumed Docta features for tabular data, assumed ground truth for \\\"rare\\\" patterns, runtime/compute constraints). Do NOT produce the full experiment design yet — I only need the inspection findings, a proposed approach sketch, and the assumptions/uncertainties list.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How can you identify rare patterns in a tabular dataset using Docta?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
