"hard sample\\\" score vs a single mixed diagnosis score affects which metric we use.\\n- Sensitivity of Docta's HLM estimation to extreme rarity (<0.5% prevalence) is unknown; the design includes rarity sweeps partly to test this, but effect sizes are not predictable in advance.\\n- Ground truth for \\\"rare\\\" on any *real* dataset would be contestable; the synthetic design sidesteps this, at the cost of external validity (a small real-dataset case study is an optional extension).\", \"evidence\": \"Environment inspection (verified via execute_check): `ls -la /workspace` shows only `task.json`; `task.json` contains the task question plus documents.track.md (\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"). `find / -iname \\\"*docta*\\\"` (two scans, including -xdev full scan) returned no matches; `python3 -c \\\"import docta\\\"` fails (ModuleNotFoundError); `pip list` contains no Docta, PyTorch, or scikit-learn; `/home/actor` and `/root` are empty; network is disabled (no way to fetch the upstream repo). Hence all Docta capability/API statements in the plan are explicitly labeled as public-documentation knowledge, not repo observations.\", \"stage\": \"plan\", \"summary\": \"Report inspection findings and propose rare-pattern design sketch\", \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact Docta API entry points, config schema, and tabular loader/score field names are unverified in this workspace and must be pinned down from the upstream repo (or researcher-supplied references) before execution.\", \"Whether the tabular path exposes a separable hard-sample score versus one fused diagnosis score is unknown; this changes which metrics apply.\", \"Behavior of Docta's latent-label/HLM estimation at extreme rarity (<0.5%) is unknown; rarity sweeps are included as diagnostics but effect sizes cannot be predicted.\", \"If the researcher wants a real public tabular dataset instead of synthetic data, a defensible operational definition of ground-truth rare patterns must